----------------------------------------------------------------------
(optional) What information can you provide about your submission that
will help your grader to grade it in the most favorable light? In
particular, what bugs are in your submission?

I had to truncate my name in the Aplus attack to K because I required
11 instructions that are 4 bytes each of shellcode but buf is 48 
bytes. Therefore, I only had 4 bytes left to use which is enough for
K + null + 2 realignment bytes.

The Aplus attacks also needs to call mprotect, which is a real 
function that works and returns, so I need a way to return to the 
shellcode after it finishes. Therefore, I need bl which saves the
address of the next instruction into register x30 before jumping, so
when mprotect executes its ret instruction, it returns back where
shellcode left off. I could not use plain b instead because mprotect
would run and x30 would contain garbage and the program would crash.
So, I had to write MiniAssembler_bl in miniassembler.c and the 
header file.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
What are your sentences from Step 1?

According to 18 U.S. Code 1030, if you were to use a buffer overrun 
attack to commit fraud or related activity in connection with 
computers, but did not attempt to cause death and did not knowingly 
or recklessly cause death, then you could receive a maximum penalty 
of 20 years in prison.

According to 18 U.S. Code 1030, if you were to use a buffer overrun 
attack to commit fraud or related activity in connection with 
computers, and attempted to cause death or knowingly or recklessly 
caused death, then you could receive a maximum penalty of life in 
prison.

